# System Diagrams

## Architecture Diagram

This diagram illustrates the high-level architecture of the multi-agent system based on the `app/` structure and schemas.

```mermaid
graph TD
    subgraph Entrypoints [UI / Entrypoints]
        CLI_Ask["ask.py (CLI User Input)"]
        CLI_Worker["worker.py (Background Job Poller)"]
        CLI_Demo["demo.py (Self-contained Demo)"]
    end

    subgraph Orchestration [Orchestration & Agents]
        Runner["app/runner.py (execute_run loop)"]
        Worker["app/worker.py (Background Daemon)"]
        Agents["app/agents.py (Supervisor, Info, Desk Agents)"]
        Tools["app/tools/hostel_tools.py (Specialized Tool Actions)"]
    end

    subgraph DataAccess [Data Access Layer]
        RunStore["app/memory.py (RunStore - Queue & State)"]
        HostelDB["app/hostel_db.py (Business Logic DAO)"]
    end

    subgraph DBs [Databases]
        AgentDB[("agent.db Schema: agent.sql")]
        BusinessDB[("hostel.db Schema: hostel.sql")]
    end

    CLI_Ask -->|Enqueues Request| RunStore
    CLI_Worker -->|Starts| Worker
    Worker -->|Claims Job| RunStore
    Worker -->|Passes Job| Runner
    Runner -->|Loads Context| RunStore
    Runner -->|Invokes| Agents
    Agents -->|Delegates to/Calls| Tools
    Tools -->|Reads/Writes| HostelDB
    Runner -->|Saves State| RunStore
    
    RunStore -->|Reads/Writes| AgentDB
    HostelDB -->|Reads/Writes| BusinessDB
```

## Database Entity-Relationship (ER) Diagrams

### `agent.db` Schema (State & Job Queue)

```mermaid
erDiagram
    thread {
        TEXT id PK
        TEXT student_id
        TEXT created_at
    }
    
    message {
        INTEGER id PK
        TEXT thread_id FK
        INTEGER seq
        TEXT role
        TEXT text
        TEXT created_at
    }

    run {
        TEXT id PK
        TEXT thread_id FK
        TEXT status
        TEXT model
        INTEGER tokens_in
        INTEGER tokens_out
        INTEGER attempts
        INTEGER max_attempts
        REAL available_at
        TEXT lease_owner
        REAL lease_until
        INTEGER cancel_requested
        TEXT error_code
        TEXT created_at
        TEXT started_at
        TEXT finished_at
    }

    run_step {
        INTEGER id PK
        TEXT run_id FK
        INTEGER seq
        TEXT kind
        INTEGER tokens_in
        INTEGER tokens_out
        TEXT text
        TEXT tool_calls
        TEXT created_at
    }

    tool_call {
        INTEGER id PK
        INTEGER run_step_id FK
        TEXT tool_name
        TEXT args
        TEXT result
        INTEGER ok
        INTEGER latency_ms
        TEXT idempotency_key
        TEXT created_at
    }

    thread ||--o{ message : "contains"
    thread ||--o{ run : "has"
    run ||--o{ run_step : "executes"
    run_step ||--o| tool_call : "triggers"
```

